course: dictionary
lesson: 7634
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is meant. The word produce is a good example. Look at the context, and check whether it is being used as a verb (a doing word) or a noun (a naming word).
explain: To produce means to make or grow something. «The factory produces 200 toys every hour.» Here produces means makes. «The farm produces apples and pears.» Here it means grows.
explain: To produce can also mean to show or bring something out. «The magician produced a rabbit from his hat.» The magician did not make the rabbit in a factory. He brought it out so everyone could see it.
explain: As a noun, produce is said PROD-yoos, with the stress at the start. «Let's buy fresh produce at the market.» Here produce means fruit and vegetables that farmers grow. Try your meaning in the sentence: fresh fruit and vegetables fit, so you know you have it right.
fact: To produce means to make or grow something, or to show or bring something out.
fact: Produce (said PROD-yoos) is a noun for fruit and vegetables that farmers grow.
fact: Plants produce oxygen, cows produce milk, and the Sun produces heat and light.
fact: «Tiny drifting algae and bacteria make roughly half of the oxygen produced on Earth.»
fact: To produce a film, show or play means to organise and pay for making it.
exercise: «The factory produces 200 toys every hour.» What does produces mean here? | Hides | *Makes | Forgets | Breaks
exercise: Mia says, «Let's buy fresh produce at the market.» What is produce? | A long walk to the shops | A type of shopping bag | A kind of market stall | *Fruit and vegetables that farmers grow
exercise: «The magician produced a rabbit from his hat.» What does produced mean here? | Made it in a factory | Hid it under a cloth | *Brought it out so everyone could see | Lost
test: «Plants produce oxygen.» Which word means the same as produce here? | Carry | *Make | Sleep | Destroy
test: In a film, to produce it means to what? | *Organise and pay for making it | Cut it into short pieces | Watch it at home | Sell tickets only
exam: Which sentence uses produce as a noun meaning fruit and vegetables? | «She produced a ticket from her bag.» | «He produced a film about dragons.» | «The factory produces toys.» | *«Let's buy fresh produce at the market.»
